# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 2: bell), edited.

~ start
solomon_roderick [weary]: The new bronze bell is stuck in deep ruts by the south footbridge, and my back gave out. The clocktower has stood dumb for a week.
* We will carry it -> accept
* Why now? -> why
* Not now -> END

~ why
solomon_roderick [neutral]: The old bell split down the seam the night the Oak last stirred. Folk lose count of the six hours without a chime.
-> start

~ accept
solomon_roderick [smile]: Bless your strong shoulders. Bring the cart to the belfry steps before the dusk mist thickens, and mind the axle in the mud.
quest weight_on_the_bell asked
set bell_asked
-> END

~ cart
Narrator: The heavy bronze bell rests under damp straw on a creaking timber cart. As you reach for the shafts, a whiskered man in a faded coat marches up.
sgt_gaunt [smile]: Halt, travellers. I held a train against forty bandits at Pipers Ford, three steps from a stand, and I shall guard this bell myself.
* Take the market lane -> market
* Take the moor road -> moor
* Let the sergeant guard it -> gaunt
* [ends:weight_on_the_bell] Abandon the cart -> abandon

~ gaunt
sgt_gaunt [smile]: Not a highwayman in Druskenvald dares cross cold steel when Sergeant Gaunt takes the vanguard.
Narrator: A rook croaks from the bridge rail, and the sergeant drops flat under the axle, clutching his hat.
sgt_gaunt [afraid]: Flanking fire from the treetops! Hold the wheel while I secure the undercarriage!
set gaunt_hired
-> cart

~ market
Narrator: Barrows, geese, and crooked lanterns crowd the market lane. A wheel drops into a gutter, tilting the bronze bell toward a stone wall.
* [Athletics DC 11] Keep the bell from tipping in the crowd -> market_ok | market_cracked

~ market_ok
Narrator: {name} braces a shoulder against the timber and heaves the cart level before the bronze kisses the wall.
set bell_route = "market"
-> stowaway

~ market_cracked
Narrator: The cart lurches and the bronze rim strikes the stone with a sour ring, cracking its lip.
set bell_cracked
set bell_route = "market"
-> stowaway

~ moor
Narrator: The outer moor road winds through black peat and mire, where sunken stones wait to snap an axle.
* [Survival DC 12] Pick the firm ground -> moor_ok | moor_slow

~ moor_ok
Narrator: {name} reads the dry heather and guides the wheels along a ridge of buried gravel.
set bell_route = "moor"
-> stowaway

~ moor_slow
Narrator: The wheels sink twice into wet peat, and dusk is fading by the time you haul the cart free.
set bell_late
set bell_route = "moor"
-> stowaway

~ stowaway
Narrator: The straw rustles, and a small boy pokes his head out, pockets clinking with loose buttons.
pip_oakum [smile]: Do not tell Solomon! I only crept in to hear the first ring from right underneath.
* Let him ride -> pip_stays
* Send him home -> pip_home
* [Perception DC 12] Notice the button trail -> pip_trail

~ pip_stays
pip_oakum [smile]: Proper good of you! I will give you a brass waistcoat button if my ears do not pop.
set bell_pip = "rides"
-> delivered

~ pip_home
pip_oakum [sad]: Aw, you sound just like Constable Squire. I am going, I am going.
set bell_pip = "home"
-> delivered

~ pip_trail
Narrator: {name} spots horn and pewter buttons dropped every ten paces down the track, with Pip's mother already marching up behind them.
pip_oakum [afraid]: Botheration, the pocket with the hole! Do not let her take my tin military ones!
set bell_pip = "found"
-> delivered

~ delivered
solomon_roderick [smile]: Safe at the belfry steps. Lend a hand on the hoist rope and hear her speak.
Narrator: The new bell swings into the dark timber tower and tolls a single, deep note over the Round.
quest weight_on_the_bell done
set bell_done
gold +30
standing brightsingers +1
-> END

~ abandon
Narrator: You leave the cart by the footbridge. By the time a hired labourer drags it to the Round, Solomon's face is set like gravestone.
solomon_roderick [angry]: A mason keeps his word, stranger. Remember that next time you offer your hands.
quest weight_on_the_bell lost
set bell_abandoned
standing brightsingers -1
-> END
